  "corrections": [
    "snd-waves.md: Bounded magnitude is not infinite arithmetic precision.",
    "snd-waves.md: Phase continuity is not a guarantee of no audible transient.",
    "snd-sampling.md: Distinguish toward-zero truncation from flooring and clipping.",
    "snd-sampling.md: The displayed experiment violates the non-overload assumption at low bit depths.",
    "snd-levels.md: Raw casts do not implement saturation.",
    "snd-measuring.md: One-sided FFT scaling must not double unpaired endpoints.",
    "snd-pitch.questions.json: Correct cents below A4; 98.7 is the interval above G4.",
    "snd-waves.questions.json: Repeated blocks have spectral lines at block-rate harmonics, not original tone plus buzz.",
    "snd-waves.questions.json: Avoid claiming phase continuity guarantees no audible transient.",
    "snd-sampling.questions.json: Explain actual experiment, not just generic coarse quantisation.",
    "snd-measuring.questions.json: Full-scale sample count is diagnostic, not definitive clipping detector.",
    "snd-measuring.questions.json: Longer captures can remain halfway between bins.",
    "snd-waves.md: Recursive oscillators and other designs need no explicit phase accumulator.",
    "snd-aliasing.questions.json: Only out-of-passband harmonics are removed during decimation.",
    "retrofit: snd-aliasing.questions.json q10: formula used the connective \"and\" as a defined symbol (\"47 and 49\"); split into separate 47 kHz / 49 kHz lines with kHz defined.",
    "retrofit: snd-waves.questions.json q3: \"0.32 × 360° ≈ 116.6°\" was arithmetically off (0.32 × 360 = 115.2); now 0.324 × 360° ≈ 116.6°.",
    "retrofit: snd-pitch.md: \"the A above 440 Hz by one semitone (A♯4)\" reworded to \"the note one semitone above A4 (440 Hz) is A♯4\".",
    "retrofit: snd-pitch.md: beat-rate In words said \"about 2.5 times a second\" against a worked 2.55 Hz; now 2.55.",
    "retrofit: snd-measuring.md: Hann window is exactly 1 in the middle only for odd N; now says \"1 (or just under 1 for even N)\".",
    "retrofit: snd-sampling.md: SQNR derivation symbols S and E now state their units.",
    "retrofit: glossary: split LSB into a new \"Least significant bit (LSB)\" entry (bit and byte senses); quantisation step keeps \"1 LSB\" only.",
    "retrofit: glossary: removed app-wide aliases that captured ordinary words or other meanings: cents, sharp edge(s), min (clashes with minutes), reference frequency, digital signal(s), codec(s), data rate, word length, unshaped, floats, fixed-point (renamed term to \"Fixed-point arithmetic\"), Fourier transform, magnitudes, Audio Engineering Society, clips, delay line.",
    "retrofit: glossary: FPU example made precise (Cortex-M4F single precision; Cortex-M7 FPU optional, single or single+double).",
    "retrofit: glossary: TPDF definition now states 2 LSB peak-to-peak and ~4.8 dB (3x noise power); MTS definition corrected to what MTS is (tuning dump / single-note retune messages); PolyBLEP attributed to Välimäki and Huovilainen 2007 with Aalto source; BLEP attributed to Brandt 2001 with its paper as source; JND definition uses the cited 3 Hz / 0.6% figures.",
    "retrofit: glossary: replaced loose sources Data_buffer (audio-block) and Coherent_sampling.",
    "retrofit: glossary: added module-04 aliases (Standard I2S, I2S port(s), codec chip(s), blocksize, line out(s)/line outputs, consumer line level, MIDI 1.0, filter cut-off, p-p, RMS voltage, kbit/s, integer full scale, sample periods, bit clocks, sample formats, μs). Skipped wrap-around, delay lines, fixed point, clip, analogue (ordinary or used with other meanings in other subjects)."
